---
export const prerender = true;
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import LegalStatus from '../components/LegalStatus.astro';
---

<Content
  kicker="Legal"
  title="Refunds & Cancellations"
  description="How refunds, cancellations, and billing disputes work on avaTOK, including app-store purchases and the rules for tokens."
  image="/og/refunds.png"
  lead="What can be refunded on avaTOK, what cannot, and how to raise a billing problem."
  updated="2026-08-28"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how refunds and cancellations work on avaTOK — our creator marketplace,
    paid live streaming, and paid 1:1 video sessions. It sits alongside
    our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, <a href="/tokens">Tokens &amp; Wallet</a> policy, and
    <a href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="status">1. Who you are dealing with</h2>
  <LegalStatus variant="full" />
  <p>
    Your agreement is with the avaTOK founding team, operating from Dehradun, Uttarakhand, India,
    under Indian law. Once we complete company registration, the registered company will take over
    these obligations and we will publish its details here. If anything on this page is unclear,
    email <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a> before you pay.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Payments are in test, and we will return anything taken in error</h2>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      avaTOK is not yet open to the public and our online payment facility is not live. Our
      application for a payment gateway as an unregistered business is <strong>under review</strong>,
      so payment and payout flows are being tested with a small number of invited users.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:12px">
      During this testing period, <strong>if any amount is charged to you in error, or a feature you
      paid to try does not work, tell us and we will refund it in full</strong> to the original
      payment method. This is deliberately more generous than the rules below, and it applies for as
      long as the service is in testing. Email
      <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>3. Tokens are generally non-refundable — but unused ones can be withdrawn</h2>
  <p>
    When you top up, your payment is converted into <a href="/tokens">tokens</a> inside the app at a
    fixed rate of <strong>1 token = ₹1 (one Indian rupee)</strong>. Tokens are the in-app unit used to
    pay for AI features and services.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      <strong>Once purchased or converted, tokens are non-refundable</strong> — except where a
      refund is required by applicable law, or by the billing policy of the app store you bought
      through (Google Play or Apple). Nothing in this policy limits rights you have that cannot be
      waived under consumer law where you live.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is about reversing a completed top-up. It does not mean your money is stuck:
      <strong>tokens you have not spent can be withdrawn</strong>, subject to verification and to
      any transfer fee and tax shown before you confirm. See section 6 and
      <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>4. Purchases made through an app store</h2>
  <p>
    If you bought a top-up or subscription inside the Android or iOS app, the payment was taken by
    the app store, not by us. Refunds for those purchases are handled by the store under its own
    policy and timelines:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Play</strong> — request a refund through your Google Play order history or
      Google Play support.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong> — request a refund through Apple's "Report a Problem" process or
      Apple Support.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We cannot reverse a store charge on your behalf. If the store approves a refund, we may reverse
    the corresponding tokens from your balance. If those tokens have already been spent, your
    balance may go to zero and your account may be restricted until the position is corrected.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Cancelling a subscription vs consuming tokens</h2>
  <p>
    These are two different things:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cancelling a recurring plan</strong> stops future charges. Cancel it wherever you
      set it up — usually the app store's subscriptions screen. Cancelling generally does not
      refund a period you have already paid for, and access normally continues until the end of the
      current period.</li>
    <li><strong>Spending tokens</strong> is immediate and is treated as consumption of the service.
      A token spent on an AI feature, a marketplace purchase, or a consultation is used up at that
      point.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Cancelling a plan does not by itself remove tokens already in your balance.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Unused vs consumed tokens</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Consumed tokens</strong> — tokens already spent on a delivered feature or service — are
    not refundable, except where required by law.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Unused tokens</strong> — tokens still sitting in your balance — may be withdrawn rather
    than refunded. They convert back at the same fixed rate they were bought at, 1 token = ₹1,
    subject to verification, the transfer fee shown at the time of withdrawal, and any tax that
    applies (including Indian GST where it is due). See
    <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Marketplace purchases and consultations</h2>
  <p>
    The marketplace and live consultancy connect you with other users who provide digital services.
    We may apply the following where a booking or order goes wrong:
  </p>
  <h3>Cancellations</h3>
  <p>
    A booking cancelled before the agreed start time may be eligible for a return of tokens to your
    balance, subject to the cancellation terms shown on the listing at the time of booking and to
    our review.
  </p>
  <h3>No-shows</h3>
  <p>
    If the provider does not attend a booked session, you may raise it with us and we may return the
    tokens to your balance. If the customer does not attend, the session may be treated as delivered
    and the tokens as consumed.
  </p>
  <h3>Failure to deliver</h3>
  <p>
    If a provider does not deliver what the listing described, tell us at
    <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>. We may review the order, withhold or
    reverse the provider's earnings, and return tokens to your balance where we consider it
    appropriate. We are not the provider of the underlying service and do not guarantee any
    particular outcome.
  </p>
  <p>
    Any resolution we make is normally in <strong>tokens returned to your balance</strong>, not a
    payment back to your card or bank.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Chargebacks</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe a charge is wrong, please contact us first — a chargeback is slower for everyone
    and may restrict your account while it is open. Where a chargeback or payment reversal is raised
    against your account, we may suspend the account, freeze the token balance, and reverse tokens
    linked to the disputed payment. We may decline further top-ups from a payment method with an
    unresolved dispute.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Fraud and abuse</h2>
  <p>
    We may refuse, reverse, or hold a refund where we reasonably suspect fraud, abuse of promotional
    credit, or a breach of our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10. How to raise a billing issue</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a> from the address on your account
    and include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your avaTOK handle or registered email;</li>
    <li>the date and amount of the charge in rupees (₹);</li>
    <li>whether you paid through Google Play, Apple, or another method;</li>
    <li>the order, booking, or transaction reference if you have one;</li>
    <li>a short description of what went wrong.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We will look into it and respond. We cannot promise a specific turnaround, and any refund we do
    make is returned by the same method that took the payment where possible.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here and revise
    the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Billing and payout questions: <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>. General
    enquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@avatok.ai">hello@avatok.ai</a>. Privacy questions:
    <a href="mailto:privacy@avatok.ai">privacy@avatok.ai</a>. See also our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
